From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: gs101: pcie0 max-link-speed 1

The modem link trains at Gen1 only; a Gen3 limit adds a 100 ms sleep after
every relink (one per CP wakeup), long enough for the CP to drop its side
of the link now and then and crash. Local.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101.dtsi
@@ -1808,7 +1808,16 @@
 			ranges = <0x82000000 0 0x40000000 0x40000000 0 0x00ff0000>;
 			bus-range = <0x00 0xff>;
 			num-lanes = <2>;
-			max-link-speed = <3>;
+			/*
+			 * The s5123 link only ever trains to Gen1 with this
+			 * PHY setup, and with a higher limit
+			 * dw_pcie_wait_for_link() sleeps another 100 ms after
+			 * link-up (PCIe r6.0 6.6.1, > 5 GT/s) on every CP
+			 * wakeup; a CP left waiting that long sometimes drops
+			 * its side of the link, the relink then never detects
+			 * the endpoint and the CP crashes. Local.
+			 */
+			max-link-speed = <1>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 472 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
 			interrupt-names = "msi";
 
